<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Barclays=E2=80=99 profits jumped in the la=
st quarter, and it gave more cash to shareholders as further bank taxes loo=
m in John Healey=E2=80=99s budget next Wednesday.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The UK lender reported a 12% rise in pre-t=
ax profits to =C2=A32.3bn for the three months to 30 September. In the UK, =
loans grew 7% year on year, with particular strength in its corporate busin=
ess, up 14%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It announced a new =C2=A3500m share buybac=
k, bringing the amount given to shareholders so far this year to =C2=A32.8b=
n, up 46% year on year.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">CS Venkatakrishnan, the Barclays chief exe=
cutive, said: =E2=80=9CI am pleased with the ongoing momentum of Barclays=
=E2=80=99 operational and financial performance.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CWith one quarter to go before the=
 end of our original three-year plan, we have either achieved or are on tra=
ck to achieve all of our 2026 group targets. We are confident in and commit=
ted to the 2028 targets that we laid out earlier in the year.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CThe investment bank delivered str=
ong equities performance, offsetting a challenging environment for FICC [fi=
xed income, currencies and commodities].</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In financial markets, the cost of French g=
overnment borrowing has increased further, hitting multidecade highs and pi=
ling pressure on ministers after weeks of increasingly violent street prote=
sts.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The yield, or interest rate, on France=E2=
=80=99s 10-year bonds rose four basis points to 5.039%, the highest since J=
uly 2002, after breaking through the 5% mark on Wednesday.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The risk premium over German Bunds has wid=
ened to 163bps, the widest since November 2011, reflecting investor concern=
s over France=E2=80=99s fiscal outlook. The government has yet to pass its =
budget.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Oil prices have climbed above $111 a barre=
l this morning, after more =E2=80=8BHouthi attacks in Saudi Arabia fuelled =
fears over an escalation of the Middle East conflict and further disruption=
s to supplies.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Brent crude, the global oil benchmark, is =
up 2.5% at $111.58 a barrel, raising fears of higher inflation, which puts =
pressure on bonds.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Asian stock markets slid, with Japan=E2=80=
=99s Nikkei down 2.65%, China=E2=80=99s CSI 300 losing 1.5% and South Korea=
=E2=80=99s Kospi tumbling 3.7%.</p>
